gpu_draw_trace_resolve_data (off by default, hot reload): while gpu_draw_trace records, every resolve is read back
synchronously (readback_resolve full) and its guest memory bytes are written to <trace>_resolves.bin with the
sequence of its trace record, so the passes of a frame can be looked at image by image. Guest memory is left as
the configured readback mode would leave it.

